<title>ISRAEL: Tadiran wins Italian air force  contract.</title>
<headline>Tadiran wins Italian air force  contract.</headline>
<dateline>JERUSALEM 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tadiran Ltd has won a tender to supply the Italian air force with an airborne search and rescue system (ASARS), the company said.</p>
<p>It said the value of the deal was $5 million.</p>
<p>The system is to be supplied by Tadiran Spectralink, a fully-owned subsidiary of Tadiran Ltd.</p>
<p>&quot;We hope to sell additional units to the Italian navy and land forces following the deal with the air force,&quot; Itzhak Beni, managing director of Tadiran Spectralink, was quoted as saying in a statement issued by the company.</p>
</text>
